<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT - Kimber cut to sell.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Kimber cut to sell.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings on Friday cut Kimberly Clark de Mexico to sell from hold due to depressed consumer demand in Mexico and decline in sale price.</p>
<p>-- Mexico equity analyst Ana Maria Mendez said Kimber's recent divestiture raised much less cash than expected. Its sales are expected to fall sharply and its reported net income is expected to drop by 26 percent year-on-year in 1997, she said.</p>
<p>((--Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
</text>
